From: Ed Maros <ed.maros@ligo.org>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] framecpp/test/CMakeLists: unify cross-compile guard across
 middle test-with-target section

The framecpp_target_executable() helper at test/CMakeLists.txt:52 early-returns
under `CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR`, and on
conda-forge's cross-compile-with-qemu arches (linux_aarch64, linux_ppc64le)
the emulator variable is passed empty to CMake even when qemu is available.
As a result many test targets (`framecpp_verify`, `test_verify_options`,
`test_serial_reader_no_toc`, `FrVectTypesTest`, ...) are silently not
created — but the many `add_test(... COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:X>)` sites
in the same file reference them unconditionally, so CMake configure
fails with e.g.:

    CMake Error at test/CMakeLists.txt:243 (add_test):
      Error evaluating generator expression:
        $<TARGET_FILE:framecpp_verify>
      No target "framecpp_verify"

The file already correctly guards two contiguous ranges (604-642 and
1271-1675) with

    if(BUILD_TESTING AND NOT ( CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR ))
    ...
    endif()

but the middle range 643-1270 is unguarded. Merge the two protected
ranges by removing the intermediate `endif()` at line 642 and the
redundant `if()` at line 1271. The `endif()` at 1675 then closes the
single outer guard that spans 604-1675, uniformly protecting every
test-target reference in that range.

Filed upstream as https://git.ligo.org/computing/ldastools/LDAS_Tools/-/issues/405.
---
 test/CMakeLists.txt | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

--- a/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -639,7 +639,6 @@
     DEPENDS ${MINIMAL_FRAME_FILES}
     COMMENT "Generating all minimal test frames for Verify class testing"
   )
-endif()

 ##-----------------------------------------------------------------------
 ## Systematic Verify Class Testing
@@ -1268,7 +1267,6 @@
 # Issue #119: also skip under cross-compile-without-emulator. The
 # test_framecpp_structure helper below adds custom commands that run
 # framecpp_sample at build time.
-if(BUILD_TESTING AND NOT ( CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR ))
   # Define frame structures to test with their minimum supported version
   # Version history based on PDFDefinitions.cc (ground truth from PDF specs):
   # - v3: FrDetector, FrHistory, FrMsg, FrSummary, FrTrigData (original name for FrEvent)
